{"id": "idaho-3", "headline": "From Kabul to Boise: Afghan women resume studies", "source": "Boise State Public Radio", "url": "https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/news/2026-11-24/womens-right-taliban-afghan-refugee-education", "published": "2026-11-24", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["Since the fall of Kabul in 2021, more than 1,000 Afghan evacuees have resettled in Idaho, most in the Boise area. Boise State Public Radio profiles two young women rebuilding their lives. Ramzia Jalali was a third semester medical student at Kabul University when the Taliban entered the city on August 15, 2021. She said she lost her hopes, her education and her life at that moment. Starting over in Boise brought steep challenges, but the city has become a refuge for young Afghan women whose schooling was cut short at home. Their stories reflect the long term work of resettlement for families who arrived five years ago. Source: Boise State Public Radio."], "qr": {"n": 37, "rows": ["1111111000011110011000101010001111111", "1000001001100110101000100110101000001", "1011101000001011100011101011001011101", "1011101010001100010001100111101011101", "1011101011000000111111111100101011101", "1000001000011010000011000110001000001", "1111111010101010101010101010101111111", "0000000000110011101010001000100000000", "1100011101010111010100000111000011000", "0100000110001011011110011111010110010", "0101101000100011101001100111111111101", "1000000001101010100010000010001000010", "0110001001011011100100101001101001011", "0010010000000101101111011011100101110", "0010011101111011011000101101001100111", "1001110100110001101010010011111110101", "1110101111011111110100100111111011101", "1101110011001001101110111001110101110", "0000001010111101011100011001001000001", "1001010100101010100110111011001001001", "1110011000101110010000100101011110111", "0111010111101011111101111111000111110", "1101111110001011010010101111111100111", "0011010000010001101000101010011011001", "011111110010100010101001000010110000